Level 8 → Level 9

Concept
This level gives you a big text file where the password is the one 
line that appears exactly once - every other line in the file is 
duplicated. The task is really about knowing how to isolate unique 
lines out of a huge block of repeated data instead of reading through 
it manually.

Commands used
ls
sort data.txt | uniq -u

Why it works
sort data.txt arranges every line alphabetically, which puts duplicate 
lines right next to each other. Piping that into uniq -u then filters 
the output down to only lines that appear exactly once - since 
duplicates get grouped together by the sort, uniq -u can spot the one 
line that has no match next to it. That line is the password.
